// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 2 „Pere, inimesed ja kirjeldamine” (a2-006…010), level A2. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline, one year before the B1
// course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia (27) has just moved to Tallinn, rents a room in Mustamäe (landlady Malle Pärn, 66) and
// learns Estonian at Keelekool Sõna (teacher Maret, administrator Ene, classmates Lucía, Dmitri, Tom). She gets to
// know her brother Jaan's family (Jaan 34, cook; Kadri, children's doctor; Mia 5; Oskar 8; the dog Muki), her uncle
// Viktor (62) and an old photo of Viktor and her mother Helgi (58, Tartu). Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end
// the learner talks about a family photo and writes a message about the family to a friend (009 Kasuta).
//   006 Sunday at Jaan's — mul on üks vend / kaks venda, mul ei ole …, nominative plural, see / need; the family tree.
//   007 things left after the visit — kelle? (genitive of names, family words, pronouns), minu oma; lost and found.
//   008 Viktor's old photo — ta on / tal on, adjective plural (pikad juuksed), comparison (pikem kui); meeting Kadri's
//       mother Tiiu at the bus station.
//   009 new people at the language school — questions about a person, retelling in the ta-form; business cards;
//       the family photo evening (final project).
// Harno A2 formats trained: short-answer listening, a letter with 3-option gaps, notices, a business card into text,
// a message ≥ 30 words, picture description with questions, question cards in pairs. Lesson 5 is the module's check
// (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/a2/module02.js.
